  "meaning": "A pattern comparator holds three deep, independent book-like pattern cassettes beside a genuine linear guide on a low machined mounting plate with rounded plan corners and flush fasteners. A large bored carriage and thick angled yoke carry a broad oxide contact tool over a recessed text ribbon. Fine graduations, short match inlays, cassette edge engravings, collars, washers, and socket screws explain storage, scanning, and the selected match position. Detailed machined construction, actual recessed marks, separate fasteners, brushed polished steel, dark red-brown granular corrosion islands with broken oxide rims, pitted normal relief and dull oxidized metal between crusts, graphite interiors, directional softbox reflections, and genuine transparent negative space.",
